solution.p:
Since the fractions dont have the same denominator, we have to make them have like denominators. Multiply the first fraction by \frac{2}{2}\text{.}
\begin{aligned}
{\frac{8}{a}+\frac{1}{2a}} \amp = {\frac{8}{a}}\cdot \frac{2}{2} + {\frac{1}{2a}}\\
\amp = \frac{16}{2a} + {\frac{1}{2a}}\\
\amp = {\frac{17}{2a}}
\end{aligned}

